window.DOCS_CONTENT = {
 "title": "Dialogue Component",
 "intro": "Everything you need to build branching, cinematic dialogue in Unreal Engine. The complete guide, hosted right here with every screenshot.",
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "getting-started",
   "num": "03",
   "icon": "🚀",
   "title": "Getting Started",
   "lede": "Add the component, paste a few nodes, and start authoring branching conversations.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"getting-started-setup\">Setup</h3><h3 id=\"getting-started-player\">Player</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1.</strong> Add the <code>Dialogue_Component</code> to your character.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/cc31df1d-6f30-458b-b7b9-576687dab6be.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/cc31df1d-6f30-458b-b7b9-576687dab6be.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>2.</strong> Copy/paste the nodes from <code>BP_DC_TPC</code> into your character blueprint.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/55ba980c-7224-4313-8641-efa486e8adce.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/55ba980c-7224-4313-8641-efa486e8adce.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"getting-started-npc\">NPC</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1.</strong> Add the <code>Dialogue_Component</code> to your NPC.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> <em>(Optional)</em> Add a <code>Camera</code> component to your NPC.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/42f607da-d484-4281-9557-f38789693ae3.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/42f607da-d484-4281-9557-f38789693ae3.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/e133e31c-b07f-413a-9cf8-e8bc7c11a23b.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/e133e31c-b07f-413a-9cf8-e8bc7c11a23b.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><p>🎉 <strong>Setup is DONE. Go customize!</strong> 🎉</p><hr><h3 id=\"getting-started-basic-dialogues\">Basic Dialogues</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1. Select Dialogue Component</strong></p><p>Click on the <strong>“Dialogue_Component”</strong> within your NPC</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/50f5d569-8505-4ae7-800b-04694d76d310.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/50f5d569-8505-4ae7-800b-04694d76d310.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>2. Open & Add Branch</strong></p><p>Open <strong>“🌿 Dialogue 🌿”</strong> and click the <strong>(➕)</strong> button</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b659784c-9163-441d-bdad-c227173f7048.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b659784c-9163-441d-bdad-c227173f7048.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The 🏁 START 🏁 variable is set to 1, meaning the dialogue will start at branch 1</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/26d03080-061a-4cc3-8d46-83f8b9d6e992.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/26d03080-061a-4cc3-8d46-83f8b9d6e992.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Since the branch is currently empty, make sure to add \"1\" to the Branch Name. Without this, the dialogue won’t start!</p></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>3. Add NPC & Player Text</strong></p><p>Add text under <strong>NPC Text</strong>:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/0742f382-5f42-486e-8a01-dd7d15aeef5f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/0742f382-5f42-486e-8a01-dd7d15aeef5f.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Add a player selection under <strong>Player</strong>:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/545d1507-81e7-4a77-84f1-067347eeb10a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/545d1507-81e7-4a77-84f1-067347eeb10a.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>Note:</strong> Since there is only one choice and it's blank, the UI shows a green continue button, similar to the <strong>Legend of Zelda</strong> dialogue style</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1c44c50f-946d-4498-b28c-c80130bc57a5.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1c44c50f-946d-4498-b28c-c80130bc57a5.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Adding even a single space in <strong>Player Text</strong> will bring back the choice format</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/2c1ad14d-888a-4490-b234-c77b3c22401a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/2c1ad14d-888a-4490-b234-c77b3c22401a.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>4. Ending the Dialogue</strong></p><p>Set <strong>“End Dialogue?”</strong> to <strong>true</strong> to close the conversation:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/23d9c44f-264a-4edc-b87c-712b126b2da4.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/23d9c44f-264a-4edc-b87c-712b126b2da4.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Next time you interact, it will reopen at <strong>Branch 1</strong>.</p></div><h3 id=\"getting-started-branching-dialogues\">Branching Dialogues</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1. Creating Multiple Branches</strong></p><p>Instead of ending our dialogue on <strong>Branch 1</strong>, set it to <strong>2</strong> and add a new branch titled <strong>“2”</strong></p><p>Repeat the previous steps, but now add <strong>two player responses</strong></p><p>The first response will continue the dialogue to <strong>Branch 3</strong></p><p>The second response will end the conversation <strong>immediately</strong> and reset back to <strong>Branch 2</strong></p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c572ceaa-fb52-4f46-9d09-af0504b194f6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c572ceaa-fb52-4f46-9d09-af0504b194f6.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>2. Adding More Branches (3 & 4)</strong></p><p>Now, add two more branches named <strong>“3”</strong> and <strong>“4”</strong>:</p><p>The first player response will loop the conversation back to <strong>Branch 1</strong>.</p><p><em>To end the conversation, set <strong>“End Dialogue?”</strong> to <strong>true</strong> or follow the sequence to close the dialogue.</em></p><p>The second response will continue to <strong>Branch 4</strong>, allowing the player to choose an <strong>“End Conversation”</strong> option.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/aa7383f2-cae2-43d2-9240-c2d64f4daead.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/aa7383f2-cae2-43d2-9240-c2d64f4daead.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "editor",
   "num": "04",
   "icon": "🖥️",
   "title": "Editor Utility Widget",
   "lede": "Keep every variable visible and preview camera angles while you build.",
   "html": "<div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The Editor Utility Widget</p><p><strong>\"EUW_DC\"</strong> keeps variables visible at all times, allowing for quick editing & previewing of camera angles.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b4a2bf69-1705-440e-a207-60d74b8d499c.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b4a2bf69-1705-440e-a207-60d74b8d499c.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><hr><h3 id=\"editor-how-to-launch\">How To Launch?</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Right-click and run the widget, select an actor, and click <strong>\"Refresh\"</strong>.</p><p>Notice how the widget will update with the dialogue properties.</p><p><</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8e50c7d5-0080-4a40-b8b8-2554392ff5bc.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8e50c7d5-0080-4a40-b8b8-2554392ff5bc.gif\" alt=\"GIF 6-5-2025 6-40-48 PM\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>></p></div><hr><h3 id=\"editor-how-to-use\">How To Use?</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The editor utility's main function is to help you edit & test changes quickly.</p><p>Any changes you make in it will be reflected in the <strong>Details</strong> panel.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/549f2f04-3f32-4ca8-a737-6d0ebb5d379b.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/549f2f04-3f32-4ca8-a737-6d0ebb5d379b.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/04033f49-fb16-48ac-a82c-86ac9ebd2d8f.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/04033f49-fb16-48ac-a82c-86ac9ebd2d8f.gif\" alt=\"GIF 6-5-2025 6-46-42 PM\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "global",
   "num": "05",
   "icon": "🛠️",
   "title": "Global Variables",
   "lede": "Apply one set of settings across every branch for simple NPCs.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"global-global-dialogue-settings\">🛠️ Global Dialogue Settings</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>When global variables is true, the settings from the structs below will be applied to all branches of dialogue.</p></div><p>This is great for very simple NPCs who will not have any complex changes when talking to them.  <br><br> Click on the <strong>“Dialogue_Component”</strong> within your NPC to customize its dialogue settings. <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p><br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> |</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8be29527-2db8-41f9-9e24-78fa174ffb65.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8be29527-2db8-41f9-9e24-78fa174ffb65.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/65881bf3-feb0-4186-b73f-4259ba9eaa35.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/65881bf3-feb0-4186-b73f-4259ba9eaa35.png\" alt=\"\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "settings",
   "num": "06",
   "icon": "⚙️",
   "title": "Additional Settings",
   "lede": "Auto-complete, activators, logs, locations, alt buttons, nameplates, visibility, and more.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"settings-auto-complete\">⚙ Auto Complete</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>⚙ <strong>Auto Complete</strong> allows dialogues to progress automatically.</p><p>You can disable input/UI for cutscene-style playback, or enable input for timed progression.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1d5feca7-1d15-4345-a8d3-262a8790e2df.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1d5feca7-1d15-4345-a8d3-262a8790e2df.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c6886632-1fc8-4324-a8a5-232f8cc6efc4.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c6886632-1fc8-4324-a8a5-232f8cc6efc4.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-activator\">🔶 Activator</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>In the Showcase level, the 🔶 Activator on Cube 1 triggers Cube 2’s dialogue.</p><p>It uses a delay of 0.2s before starting branch 1.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a14ad12a-8231-4b24-8454-31faad531527.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a14ad12a-8231-4b24-8454-31faad531527.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1b9cb6e8-7554-4d34-9bd5-97605088628d.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1b9cb6e8-7554-4d34-9bd5-97605088628d.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-destroy\">💥 Destroy</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>💥 <strong>Destroy</strong> lets you remove the actor or its interaction ring on a specified branch (e.g., \"Destroy\").</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/16c94541-489b-4bc4-9e22-5b000ca512c3.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/16c94541-489b-4bc4-9e22-5b000ca512c3.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-logs\">💬 Logs</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Dialogue logs show past NPC and player responses.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/e83bc512-dc55-42aa-8104-9633d88f8ff0.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/e83bc512-dc55-42aa-8104-9633d88f8ff0.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/af6eacf9-6195-417f-846d-312f024f2f5a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/af6eacf9-6195-417f-846d-312f024f2f5a.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/4defd179-4ae6-4391-9964-b4bc324e656f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/4defd179-4ae6-4391-9964-b4bc324e656f.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/52dde1de-fadf-4707-b54f-760a71f1c062.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/52dde1de-fadf-4707-b54f-760a71f1c062.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-location\">🌍 Location</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Two types of location settings: player teleport and NPC movement.</p><p>If <strong>Player Move To Location</strong> is true and a <code>BP_PlayerLocation</code> is present, player teleports to it during dialogue.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/261b4b68-b54b-4018-b1a0-307800092787.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/261b4b68-b54b-4018-b1a0-307800092787.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/412c3f65-e6f3-4fc6-8c15-96a0522a2333.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/412c3f65-e6f3-4fc6-8c15-96a0522a2333.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>NPCs can also move to locations on interaction.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/5f0b0678-f5c0-48d4-a8bb-ba605b923c3f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/5f0b0678-f5c0-48d4-a8bb-ba605b923c3f.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If <strong>Use Global</strong> is true, movement occurs on all interactions. If false, movement happens only on specified branches.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b5de7e0b-73d0-4712-99cc-762263e20916.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b5de7e0b-73d0-4712-99cc-762263e20916.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can also attach <code>BP_PlayerLocation</code> to your character to preview where the player will appear.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/12012d47-8a85-43f8-8538-c61a1d9f615a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/12012d47-8a85-43f8-8538-c61a1d9f615a.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Press <strong>Refresh</strong> to generate a preview mesh that displays the player’s set location and rotation in-game.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c4703e7d-b4b0-4ddc-a4e9-90aadb25d785.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c4703e7d-b4b0-4ddc-a4e9-90aadb25d785.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-animations-audio\">🤺 Animations & 🔊 Audio</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Animations and sounds can be added through ➕ Extra Settings.</p><p>You can add multiple entries—arrays support multi-action playback.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/28fe1863-70ac-4785-977c-de8f389f4b4d.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/28fe1863-70ac-4785-977c-de8f389f4b4d.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>These settings are also editable in the Editor Utility.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/9e75ff87-479f-4cae-9b3a-b248176a6bd8.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/9e75ff87-479f-4cae-9b3a-b248176a6bd8.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-alternative-buttons\">🎮 Alternative Buttons</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>An alternative input system is available for dialogue choices, inspired by games like <em>Telltale</em>, <em>Detroit: Become Human</em>, and <em>Oxenfree</em>.</p><p>Instead of one button for all choices, this system allows separate inputs per option.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/94e74d98-54e5-47ea-a697-1631be3ff576.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/94e74d98-54e5-47ea-a697-1631be3ff576.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>To use it, enable <strong>Use Buttons?</strong> in the settings.</p><p>Default keys are 1–4 on keyboard and A/B/X/Y on Xbox controller.</p><p>If used with Auto Complete, the system will randomly choose an available option when the timer ends.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/7b5b2ba6-21fd-4df4-bc2b-a313a0e57533.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/7b5b2ba6-21fd-4df4-bc2b-a313a0e57533.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Button layouts, input bindings, and visual styles can be customized in the <strong>🎮 Alt Button</strong> struct.</p><p>The NPC using this system must include the <code>W_Alt_Buttons</code> widget and its logic.</p><p>A complete setup is already implemented in a sample NPC. Duplicate or create a child for your own use.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/580e3f1f-fd8f-482a-84cf-30928c5341ff.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/580e3f1f-fd8f-482a-84cf-30928c5341ff.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-nameplate-ui\">🏷️ Nameplate UI</h3><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/feace594-20db-4e73-8808-4beba52de021.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/feace594-20db-4e73-8808-4beba52de021.png\" alt=\"\"></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>When the bool is set to true, the below settings are applied to the current branch.</p><p>The example below first starts with the NPC preset, shows both sprites, and focuses on the right sprite.</p><p>The next branch uses the Player preset, both sprites, and uses the left sprite.</p><p>_<strong>⚠️ The preview window may not perfectly reflect what is shown in gameplay ⚠️</strong>_</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/5f93954f-9f12-456a-9785-6a3a5ed3b160.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/5f93954f-9f12-456a-9785-6a3a5ed3b160.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can edit the preset properties under the preset struct within the component.</p><p>After setting the properties in the preset window, just put the name of the preset to use in the editor utility and it will be selected.</p><p>_<strong>To darken a sprite, simply adjust the tint so that it's darker.</strong>_</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/7ba1cdad-fc94-43f8-a621-97c775549cd5.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/7ba1cdad-fc94-43f8-a621-97c775549cd5.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-visibility\">👁️ Visibility</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can change the visibility of the player and the actor they’re talking to by enabling the appropriate settings in the <strong>Dialogue Component</strong>.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/999465ce-f166-4fbb-ac2b-2b746af0373e.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/999465ce-f166-4fbb-ac2b-2b746af0373e.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>For modular characters composed of multiple body parts (children), set <strong>Propagate to Children</strong> to <code>true</code> to ensure visibility is applied consistently.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1381f09e-a21e-4d2c-8eef-3644e57cad61.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1381f09e-a21e-4d2c-8eef-3644e57cad61.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>⚠️ Attached objects (like weapons, scrolls, or accessories) may inherit visibility settings unexpectedly.</p><p>In this example, the player has a scroll and an icon attached.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1eefbe3f-c1bc-45ec-9a1f-e3fbfe0dcc95.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1eefbe3f-c1bc-45ec-9a1f-e3fbfe0dcc95.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>When dialogue begins, everything disappears as expected. But when it ends, unintended elements (like the logo) may reappear.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/83528d39-38e5-406a-8c8f-b50621791b5e.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/83528d39-38e5-406a-8c8f-b50621791b5e.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>To prevent this, add specific tags to the <strong>Visibility Tags</strong> array. Only components with those tags will be affected.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/f5c5e19e-6dda-4c8f-b61f-44f213041497.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/f5c5e19e-6dda-4c8f-b61f-44f213041497.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>In this case, we added the tag <strong>\"Visibility\"</strong> to both the player and the NPC.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/94a691cb-65ac-40f9-9b50-1aaef1027c9c.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/94a691cb-65ac-40f9-9b50-1aaef1027c9c.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>✅ Now, when the dialogue ends, the scroll and icon no longer reappear.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/311cd1a9-3dfc-4a27-8b9f-b7e3801ba0be.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/311cd1a9-3dfc-4a27-8b9f-b7e3801ba0be.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-skip-branch\">⏩ Skip Branch</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The <strong>\"E\" key</strong> is used for dialogue interactions.</p><p>A bool can register a regular input as a skip.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/2954845a-59b5-4a53-a672-b6ae4f5b88f1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/2954845a-59b5-4a53-a672-b6ae4f5b88f1.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>A new field under 🎭 <strong>Player Choices</strong> lets you specify a branch for the skip button.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/94eec95a-ad0b-4e0f-8592-a4714ca67fe0.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/94eec95a-ad0b-4e0f-8592-a4714ca67fe0.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Setting <strong>Skip To Branch</strong> to <code>3</code> makes the player get thanked for a purchase (even if none was made).</p><p>Adding <code>[end]</code> immediately after the branch (no spaces) ends dialogue and resumes at the specified branch.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/194c4f8e-d597-48fc-93d6-87dc822b7c30.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/194c4f8e-d597-48fc-93d6-87dc822b7c30.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If left blank, the skip input will default to the regular branch tied to the player's selected choice.</p><p>You can also delete the skip input from the widget if you don’t want it available.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ad036f0a-4ab2-45c2-9cd2-efc4fd088274.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ad036f0a-4ab2-45c2-9cd2-efc4fd088274.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "conditions",
   "num": "07",
   "icon": "⚖️",
   "title": "Conditions",
   "lede": "Gate responses on player stats with pass / fail states.",
   "html": "<div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ddbce72d-2e35-4835-a1cd-b471d6b99588.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ddbce72d-2e35-4835-a1cd-b471d6b99588.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Each player response includes a <strong>Player Conditions</strong> struct.</p><p>This struct defines conditions that must be met for the response to be valid.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/348d6043-a436-4a80-9958-9f96782f007b.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/348d6043-a436-4a80-9958-9f96782f007b.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>In <strong>DC_Demo</strong>, the Shop NPC sells beer for 3 gold.</p><p>The condition checks if <strong>Gold ≥ 3</strong>, then subtracts and moves to Branch 3. If false, it moves to Branch 4.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/e6df9909-884f-448d-a6c1-ea8180361a45.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/e6df9909-884f-448d-a6c1-ea8180361a45.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>In <strong>DC_Interrogation</strong>, the first response is grayed out.</p><p>The system checks for <strong>Evidence ≥ 1</strong> and the <strong>Fail State</strong> is set to <strong>Deactivate</strong>.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c02c30ae-baeb-4f9c-9fa5-2228392744b6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c02c30ae-baeb-4f9c-9fa5-2228392744b6.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c09bb67b-afb1-44e3-b582-3eb079a5c8db.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c09bb67b-afb1-44e3-b582-3eb079a5c8db.png\" alt=\"\"></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>Button Fail States</strong>:</p><p>• <em>Nothing</em>: Fully interactable</p><p>• <em>Deactivate</em>: Grayed out</p><p>• <em>Hide</em>: Completely hidden</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c811a45d-4717-4003-8068-53270f15ec67.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c811a45d-4717-4003-8068-53270f15ec67.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>After changing the fail state to <strong>Hide</strong>, the first option disappears entirely.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a9106500-a846-47a3-9af8-57f93ad27eb9.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a9106500-a846-47a3-9af8-57f93ad27eb9.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "rich-text",
   "num": "08",
   "icon": "🎨",
   "title": "Rich Text, Icons & Fonts",
   "lede": "Style text inline with color tags, icons, and custom fonts.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"rich-text-rich-text-icons\">🎨 Rich Text & Icons</h3><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/819cdf26-6efb-456a-ba31-e993f301fad7.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/819cdf26-6efb-456a-ba31-e993f301fad7.png\" alt=\"\"></div><p><br> These data tables contain the tags used with Rich Text blocks to add stylized fonts and icons in text widgets. <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> The text below is how you use rich text and icon decorators. <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> <strong>Tag Format:</strong> DB = Default Blue DG = Default Green IR = Italics Red BY = Bold Yellow <br><br> <strong>Icon Format:</strong> Talk1 = <img class=\"inline-icon\" src=\"assets/docs/da3aa086-3738-4632-ac5b-b0daebf223d0.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/da3aa086-3738-4632-ac5b-b0daebf223d0.png\" alt=\"\"> Talk2 = <img class=\"inline-icon\" src=\"assets/docs/769ba7f1-0f29-4a78-8df9-cd2cc450f988.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/769ba7f1-0f29-4a78-8df9-cd2cc450f988.png\" alt=\"\"> Map__ = <img class=\"inline-icon\" src=\"assets/docs/4d24c934-a265-4c47-868a-7daf6a7e1c9f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/4d24c934-a265-4c47-868a-7daf6a7e1c9f.png\" alt=\"\"> |</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a298e7a3-4cbb-4356-a0e3-3de3d7b0753f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a298e7a3-4cbb-4356-a0e3-3de3d7b0753f.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/fcfe3e38-26b1-4d31-9330-ba54b0ccaa80.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/fcfe3e38-26b1-4d31-9330-ba54b0ccaa80.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/3136b4c7-c1a3-4545-aea8-0785a2d9faa9.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/3136b4c7-c1a3-4545-aea8-0785a2d9faa9.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/82240f17-0f1c-44eb-9753-a4d0a21a10cc.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/82240f17-0f1c-44eb-9753-a4d0a21a10cc.png\" alt=\"\"></div><hr><h3 id=\"rich-text-font-settings\">🅰️ Font Settings</h3><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c20317d6-412b-4bd0-b98c-76003df20c4a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c20317d6-412b-4bd0-b98c-76003df20c4a.png\" alt=\"\"></div><p><br> You can easily edit all fonts by opening this asset and assigning your custom fonts. <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> ⚠️ <strong>Important:</strong> Occasionally, changes won’t appear until you restart your project. <br><br> 🔠 Font Size <br> A proper in-editor solution is not yet available. <br><br> For now, link a spreadsheet to manage font sizes manually. <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> |</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/6d020a64-0b2a-4523-a32f-117fc3a2a565.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/6d020a64-0b2a-4523-a32f-117fc3a2a565.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/49a5cc10-f563-468b-b42a-5b89c75ac286.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/49a5cc10-f563-468b-b42a-5b89c75ac286.png\" alt=\"\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "ui",
   "num": "09",
   "icon": "🎛️",
   "title": "UI Customization",
   "lede": "Two ways to restyle the dialogue UI, with live preview.",
   "html": "<p>UI can be set 2 ways:</p><h4>1. Modify the widget blueprints</h4><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>🔧 Widget Modification Control</p></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If you plan to modify values using the widgets, set this <strong>bool to false</strong>. This prevents overrides and allows manual control through the UI.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/fe7b5816-7802-4c04-8501-c5735e9c2b66.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/fe7b5816-7802-4c04-8501-c5735e9c2b66.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h4>2. Utilize the properties exposed below</h4><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The <strong>UI Presets</strong> struct contains several ready-to-use UI styles.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/eb64f741-8354-403b-8aa5-665aa667ccf2.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/eb64f741-8354-403b-8aa5-665aa667ccf2.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>These can be previewed and adjusted in real time.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/4521bdf8-076b-4cf0-86ce-055571d0d79e.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/4521bdf8-076b-4cf0-86ce-055571d0d79e.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Live changes allow you to see your edits instantly.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/9588b33b-b8b1-4818-a2e9-2f623882dd92.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/9588b33b-b8b1-4818-a2e9-2f623882dd92.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can also manually edit the struct properties here.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/606928d3-28d6-4960-bc0b-870c78f7d044.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/606928d3-28d6-4960-bc0b-870c78f7d044.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "save",
   "num": "10",
   "icon": "💾",
   "title": "Save System",
   "lede": "Persist actor transforms, branches, and conditions, then restore them on load.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"save-overview\">Overview</h3><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/9865478c-94a0-4094-9078-8931989c95a9.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/9865478c-94a0-4094-9078-8931989c95a9.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><p>The DC Save Ref object is where various properties are saved, such as actor location and the branches each actor was left on</p><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The properties are saved in the struct and can be extracted like this</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/3e947398-ac34-4d2d-a4e4-444e3b90f1e4.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/3e947398-ac34-4d2d-a4e4-444e3b90f1e4.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If you are going to use this asset's save file, ensure you set these bools to true on the Player's Dialogue Component's Save Struct</p><p>If you don't, the struct will still be updated throughout your play session (and can be used for your own save system if you're using one)</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/fa2b6d0f-667e-4ed2-b9e5-a1cecd236f04.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/fa2b6d0f-667e-4ed2-b9e5-a1cecd236f04.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><h3 id=\"save-explanation\">Explanation</h3><h3 id=\"save-saving\">💾 Saving</h3><p>Saving is a tricky thing to grasp at first, so this may be difficult to understand until you get it down.</p><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Let's start with the custom events that come with the default BP_DC_TPC</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c03afbdc-f3b9-45f2-96bc-eba104b138da.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c03afbdc-f3b9-45f2-96bc-eba104b138da.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Here we have several functions that utilize the save logic when these keys are pressed</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/759cd502-1e0e-45e5-ad8f-bbbc3f48bf0d.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/759cd502-1e0e-45e5-ad8f-bbbc3f48bf0d.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The way \"Save Game\" works is if a save slot doesn't exist, one is created, and when created, it saves the data from all actor transforms, their current START branches, and conditions into the DC Save REF's struct</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/346249a8-d08e-4fd5-acf1-43cee14fe739.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/346249a8-d08e-4fd5-acf1-43cee14fe739.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><p>The image below shows in the first comment box, that the system loops through every actor and checks if they have the Dialogue Component</p><p>For all the actors that do, the next comment box gets their transforms added to the DC Save Ref's struct, as well as their current START (branch), and the player's conditions</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/38eef28a-e77d-4180-8ac4-bc874656bd1f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/38eef28a-e77d-4180-8ac4-bc874656bd1f.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><h3 id=\"save-loading\">💿 Loading</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>When the \"Load\" event is called, the system extracts the data from the DC Save Ref's struct and sets the properties for each actor</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b5041f37-c496-491f-9042-fa3c3da06f5e.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b5041f37-c496-491f-9042-fa3c3da06f5e.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/3bc35a15-0f8c-417d-b3c0-e212a84b3c4a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/3bc35a15-0f8c-417d-b3c0-e212a84b3c4a.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><p>For example, within the \"Set Transforms\" collapsed node, we can see that DC Save REF's structs \"Actor Transform\" map is used to load up each actor & their transform data that was previously saved, and sets their transform using it, restoring it to exactly how it was when the player saved the game.</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1f9ce004-1a4c-47e8-940f-9fc1f02749ea.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1f9ce004-1a4c-47e8-940f-9fc1f02749ea.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><p>The same occurs when the system loads up each actor's START branch</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/5199347c-ff40-4dce-b3b6-290f0708e793.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/5199347c-ff40-4dce-b3b6-290f0708e793.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><h3 id=\"save-using-with-other-assets\">🧩 Using With Other Assets</h3><p>When using save systems from other assets, you basically want to call upon either the entire, or partial parts of the save and load logic from the Dialogue Component</p><p>So if another asset has a save button, you'd add the Dialogue Componeont's save logic, and same for loading</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "moving-actor",
   "num": "11",
   "icon": "🎬",
   "title": "Moving Actor & Camera Tracker",
   "lede": "Spline-driven cinematic rails and consistent camera framing.",
   "html": "<div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>🎬 BP_MovingActor</p></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><code>BP_MovingActor</code> is a multifunctional actor for camera control and interactive movement.</p><p>It supports <strong>Look At</strong> targets, fade effects, and focus settings.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/95156fc1-2747-46fd-ab8a-9a0122ca78b7.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/95156fc1-2747-46fd-ab8a-9a0122ca78b7.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>It can move along spline paths, functioning as a cinematic rail, platform, door, or elevator.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/5545a3cd-d9e6-4999-9b92-d1a6437455b7.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/5545a3cd-d9e6-4999-9b92-d1a6437455b7.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can also assign an actor to trigger a branch change after the spline finishes—useful for reaction-based events.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a9e80284-3515-4a1e-8450-b6b72bae7ade.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a9e80284-3515-4a1e-8450-b6b72bae7ade.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>A 🎯 Target Actor can follow the spline path. See the Showcase level for an example: a helicopter flying through the scene via spline movement.</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>🎥 BP_CameraTracker</p></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><code>BP_CameraTracker</code> works like <code>BP_PlayerLocation</code>. Add it to your actor.</p><p>If it’s the target of a <code>BP_MovingActor</code>, the camera will look at this point while tracking movement.</p><p>Ideal for scenarios where LookAt offsets aren’t consistent across characters.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b453cd40-7a7e-4a4d-8a3c-af4583710b28.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b453cd40-7a7e-4a4d-8a3c-af4583710b28.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "data-tables",
   "num": "12",
   "icon": "📊",
   "title": "Data Tables",
   "lede": "Author whole conversations in a spreadsheet and import them by name.",
   "html": "<p>Sample CSV <a href=\"https://mega.nz/file/NbMlkAKY#eqJEnkJHq2ZPZgz6hJZQrt3DJ_yg_Yqw7KzslqJmsL0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a></p><h3 id=\"data-tables-1-overview\">1. Overview</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can make dialogues in a spreadsheet and import them in.</p><p>Here I've added the NPC_DataTable actor and we can see that there are no branches.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/decd1213-956a-4785-9300-b9ca519c1330.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/decd1213-956a-4785-9300-b9ca519c1330.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ba8544f1-f9c3-4004-80cf-3fbba4e2116d.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ba8544f1-f9c3-4004-80cf-3fbba4e2116d.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If we open up the <strong>DT_Dialogue</strong> Data Table asset, we can see a sample dialogue.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ce809d2c-aca9-4fa0-a76c-77684f0cb0c8.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ce809d2c-aca9-4fa0-a76c-77684f0cb0c8.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><p>It is currently linked to a CSV file which allows for easy updating.</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/3d2229c5-f9e2-47f9-96a4-1e16c8618687.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/3d2229c5-f9e2-47f9-96a4-1e16c8618687.png\" alt=\"\"></div><p>To import, ensure a data table asset is loaded and press the \"Import\" button. When it's complete, you'll see the branch # update.</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/bb5a9f2d-943e-49ec-8cb3-985af5ca6fc8.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/bb5a9f2d-943e-49ec-8cb3-985af5ca6fc8.gif\" alt=\"\"></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Pressing the \"Import\" button with a file path specified will: 1. Update the data table and, 2. populate the Dialogue Component with the respective branches.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/363954d1-031e-4e3d-b26a-9024546ee501.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/363954d1-031e-4e3d-b26a-9024546ee501.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If no file path is specified, it will simply populate with the existing Data Table and not update it.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a388b999-236f-4a6c-bb6f-3d673833550d.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a388b999-236f-4a6c-bb6f-3d673833550d.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can export the data table asset as a CSV by right-clicking and selecting <strong>Export</strong>, and then work on it with an external program like Excel.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8a0c7357-612d-4811-bb68-9c376fccfca2.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8a0c7357-612d-4811-bb68-9c376fccfca2.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><hr><p>🟩 Only branches with the \"START\" column filled will populate.<br><br> 🟧 For choices, copy the \"START\" branch and name the \"Speaker\" 'Choice' followed by a number for each choice.<br><br> Branch 3 has 4 rows, and after the first, speaker names become choices.<br><br> Each column represents a property of the branch/choice.<br><br> 🟪 For booleans, type \"t\" to set them to true.<br><br> 🟨 For audio/animations, add the asset name, and the system will find it in the Content Browser.</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c5a0fb37-acd7-4877-a9d2-854fbbd75b62.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c5a0fb37-acd7-4877-a9d2-854fbbd75b62.png\" alt=\"\"></div><p><strong>You can space out your rows for better organization as empty rows will be skipped!</strong></p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/f9a63fce-800f-42cf-bbba-d4c23830df36.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/f9a63fce-800f-42cf-bbba-d4c23830df36.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><p>Conditions must be formatted like below: <br><br><code>((\"Energy\", 1),(\"Money\", 5))</code></p><p>If you're ever unsure, you can open the data table asset in Unreal and update properties there, then export and you'll see how things should be formatted.</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a1cb5735-c85b-4cb2-8c7b-03cc20832f99.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a1cb5735-c85b-4cb2-8c7b-03cc20832f99.gif\" alt=\"\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "faq",
   "num": "02",
   "icon": "❓",
   "title": "FAQ & Troubleshooting",
   "lede": "Fixes for movement, interaction visuals, and hair groom issues.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"faq-cant-move\">🚫 Can't Move?</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If you cannot move in the asset’s levels, it may be because Unreal Engine 5.1+ uses <b>Enhanced Input</b> instead of the older Input Actions.</p><p>METHOD 1</p><p>In the demo character, there’s a grouped node containing a comment with enhanced inputs:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/d9bdcac7-0ade-445e-886d-c9ea499f9db6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/d9bdcac7-0ade-445e-886d-c9ea499f9db6.png\" alt=\"Enhanced Input Example\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Copy/paste this node group anywhere in the Blueprint, and then you should be able to move around with the character:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/2add6f58-8392-4d31-8020-e2f945d98346.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/2add6f58-8392-4d31-8020-e2f945d98346.png\" alt=\"Blueprint Placement Example\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div></div><p><br><br>METHOD 2 <br><br>You can import the default inputs via <strong>Project Settings → Input</strong>, or download the preset config files:<br><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://mega.nz/file/JPkHFKqL#qfZGzDph4j6H_jMm832cXOBdoCDDdXjsV6HY7VJPi9s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Download Default Inputs</a><br><br><p align=\"center\"></p><p align=\"center\"></p> |</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a938dc34-9d0e-42d2-9188-60439f1cf880.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a938dc34-9d0e-42d2-9188-60439f1cf880.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/322d47ee-033a-4a0f-b003-de7fc8166f83.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/322d47ee-033a-4a0f-b003-de7fc8166f83.png\" alt=\"\"></div><h3 id=\"faq-remove-outline-icon-interaction-ring\">🧼 Remove Outline, Icon, Interaction Ring</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>To disable interaction visuals like the outline, icon, or ring:</p><p>Select your NPC’s <strong>Dialogue Component</strong>, and set the following bools to <code>false</code>:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/0e7df6e4-8287-49a3-a971-bcfc0000278c.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/0e7df6e4-8287-49a3-a971-bcfc0000278c.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8c24989a-d95b-4011-87d7-c652c2ee5179.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8c24989a-d95b-4011-87d7-c652c2ee5179.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ce487df5-e861-45bf-bb5e-19775c5982e6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ce487df5-e861-45bf-bb5e-19775c5982e6.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"faq-hair-groom-turns-red-afro\">💇 Hair Groom Turns Red / Afro?</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If your character’s Groom component turns red or deforms when starting dialogue, apply the fix below:</p><p>✅ <strong>How to fix:</strong> Click the hair groom component → set <code>Override Settings = true</code> and <code>Enable Simulation = true</code></p><p>❓ <strong>Why it happens:</strong> Cause is unknown, but this resolves it.</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8f677549-6122-4766-8217-d1798ac950a0.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8f677549-6122-4766-8217-d1798ac950a0.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/0d4b7596-b845-433b-9477-29dddbd5d4ee.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/0d4b7596-b845-433b-9477-29dddbd5d4ee.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "changelog",
   "num": "01",
   "icon": "🗒️",
   "title": "Change Log",
   "lede": "Every update, newest first.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"changelog-2132026\">2/13/2026</h3><ul><li>Added binding on actor destroyed, destroy interaction ring (when destroying actor outside of dialogue)</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-2102026\">2/10/2026</h3><ul><li>Added bools to save settings, allowing you to toggle whether or not load certain properties</li><li>Fixed Action example in the demo level (actor who opens the door) so that if using save, the door is raised even if you exited dialogue/game before it finished opening</li><li>Fixed \"Apply to all\" function: it would completely remove any dialogue audio you had for each branch</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-12142025\">12/14/2025</h3><ul><li>Added In World Dialogue widget display (for things like non-important dialogue/actors)</li><li>Added logic to start auto complete upon text display completing (before auto complete would begin immediately, even if text was still being typed. Would result in completing typed text, not progressing it. Doesn't effect instant text)</li><li>Fixed save game for picks (bp scroll would get destroyed but not save, now it does</li><li>Added save game logic to save actors using \"Talk Once\"</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-11252025\">11/25/2025</h3><ul><li>Removed unnecessary Debug variables (so struct directly influences)</li><li>Removed unnecessary Name variables (so struct directly influences)</li><li>Removed unnecessary Trace variables (so struct directly influences)</li><li>Added ability to assign camera by name on data table import</li><li>Added pass & fail conditions, that way you can easily adjust conditions</li><li>Improved Editor Utility interface</li><li>Improved Editor Utility speed</li><li>Fixed warning log about scrollbox</li><li>Fixed warning about spawning from empty class</li><li>Fixed tool tip to work even on disabled buttons (useful for letting player know why a choice is unable to be selected)</li><li>Fixed conditions bug on continue choices</li><li>Fixed icon widget visibility (it was blocking mouse input for alt buttons)</li><li>Fixed bug when going from overlapping auto start not destroying self if begin talking to another actor</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-9222025\">9/22/2025</h3><ul><li>Fixed interaction ring not reappearing upon dialogue ending</li><li>Added individual collapsible variable groups in editor utility</li><li>Added logic to stop montage when dialogue finishes (useful when animation was full body, because you'd move and legs would be stiff)</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-9112025\">9/11/2025</h3><ul><li>Added logic so that refreshing widget will automatically select dialogue component in your details panel</li><li>Test condition choices in preview widget</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-9102025\">9/10/2025</h3><ul><li>Added ability to interact with dialogue in editor preview</li><li>Added ability to scale UI & preview window with mouse & keyboard</li><li>Added Function Typer</li><li>Added keyboard shortcuts</li><li>Added arrow key & d-pad inputs</li><li>[Control + P] Toggle preview window</li><li>[Alt + R] Refreshes selected</li><li>[Arrow Left/Right] Previous/Next branch</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-912025\">9/1/2025</h3><ul><li>Added a comment of 5.1+ enhanced inputs to paste instead of needing to import default inputs</li><li>Updated \"On Specific Branch\" macro to allow for a pin to specify which actor's dialogue component to use (leaving empty works as is, checking owning actor's dialogue component</li><li>Added new BML that will check for any or specific # of condition properties</li><li>Fixed bug where non-choice button showed up as a choice after talking to a choice-based actor</li><li>Fixed crashing due to old editor utility</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-632025\">6/3/2025</h3><p>> [!TIP] > Updated Rich Text / Icons to work with any text length<br> > Added logic to hide/disable choices if player doesn't meet conditions<br></p><p>> [!CAUTION] > <code>UI</code> folder has been renamed to <code>Textures</code> <br></p><ul><li>Removed selected actor reference in editor utility, allowing you to delete without the reference window popping up</li><li>Added logic for button input running when released instead of pressed, and pressing and dragging off the button then releasing will negate input</li><li>Cleaned up editor utility logic so preview camera reflects current branch camera</li><li>Fixed accessed none error when importing data tables</li><li>Removed unnecessary variable filters in editor utility</li><li>Pinned top portion of editor utility</li><li>Fixed issue where ending dialogue outside the dialogue ring wasn't re-enabling interaction</li><li>Added widget preview to the editor utility</li><li>Fixed primary and secondary logs and added enum drop-down to select which to use</li><li>Fixed moving actor construct script warnings</li><li>Moved BP_MovingActor to main blueprints folder</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-412025\">4/1/2025</h3><ul><li>Added 'skip' button</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-3262025\">3/26/2025</h3><ul><li>Added <a href=\"https://github.com/dylogaming/Dialogue-Component/wiki/24.-Data-Tables\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Data Table</a> documentation</li><li>Code cleanup in Editor Utility</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-3102025\">3/10/2025</h3><ul><li>Cleaned up blueprint-created dialogue macros</li><li>Added \"Start Dialogue Externally\" node which allows you to trigger dialogues of any specified actor that has DC</li><li>Added enum on player choices to allow you to reset NPC rotation to original facing direction when choice is made (you'd typically use this on dialogue end)</li><li>Fixed continue button being flipped on default and flipping when hovering</li><li>Fixed continue button colors not being applied when adding a texture</li><li>Reverted BP_Combat blueprint to default settings (I had tweaked the blueprint when testing with it in the test level, modifying the one in the Dialogue_Blueprints level)</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-242025\">2/4/2025</h3><ul><li>Optimized textures, reducing overall asset size</li><li>Added macros to allow for dialogue creation & branch updating using blueprints in editor & runtime</li><li>Added pseudo-dialogue tree templates</li><li>Added bool to allow you to use UI struct or edit dialogue widget blueprint directly</li><li>Made it so rich text will type 1 character at a time (before it would auto-fill and only type default letters 1 at a time)</li><li>Fixed issue where if using \"Set actor location\" to true on multiple branches would sometimes put the player through the ground</li><li>Updated Player Location mesh to an arrow instead of a ball, allowing you to tell what direction the player will face</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-172025\">1/7/2025</h3><ul><li>Visibility tag array added, allowing you to specify which parts of an actor you want to adjust visibility</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-12262024\">12/26/2024</h3><ul><li>Added scrollbox to editor utility widget, allowing for better usability</li><li>Converted nameplate & sprite images back to object variables allowing for animated sprites</li><li>Added functionality for animated sprites</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-1292024\">12/9/2024</h3><ul><li>Added variable to play level sequences & set options under ➕ Extra Settings for both player & NPC</li></ul><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b1e31413-3b79-441b-afa2-df8e30f60c9f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b1e31413-3b79-441b-afa2-df8e30f60c9f.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><h3 id=\"changelog-10242024\">10/24/2024</h3><ul><li>Fixed bug where \"start on overlap\" dialogues that ended on the same branch would result in looping the convo</li><li>Fixed Nameplate & Sprite NPCs from causing issues with UI</li><li>Fixed bug where \"Hide UI this branch\" being true would flash on ending dialogue</li><li>Cleared default \"Name Search\" replacement from default being \"Player\" because it would constantly get changed in default example dialogues</li><li>Updated object references to soft references in BP_MovingActor (increases efficiency & allows you to save instance selected to blueprint w/o issue)</li><li>Fixed Showcase level \"ally\" dialogue not updating after opening the gate</li><li>Fixed bug where overlapping another actor while current dialogue plays wasn't ending current one and starting overlapped one</li><li>Alt button choices now use the UI Preset (still going to work on this more)</li><li>Alt buttons can be clicked on with mouse</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-10222024\">10/22/2024</h3><ul><li>Added validation to mesh variables allowing for 2D paper characters to work</li><li>Removed \"look at player\" bool from camera struct since it's no longer being used</li><li>Added tool tips to camera struct properties</li><li>Cleaned up Wraith in demo area</li><li>Fixed bug where attached cine cameras (not preset ones) wouldn't be used</li><li>Added scroll box style variable so you can easily hide edge shadows</li><li>Changed \"Fade In/Out\" to Fade & updated code to forward/reverse</li><li>Added fade out of dialogue UI</li><li>Removed Event Tick from Dialogue Widget (Wasn't even being used 🤦🏻‍♂️)</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-9192024\">9/19/2024</h3><ul><li>Added ability to import data tables which can format into branches</li></ul><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c9d237e8-e1c1-4849-b353-dbb586e995eb.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c9d237e8-e1c1-4849-b353-dbb586e995eb.gif\" alt=\"GIF 9-19-2024 5-45-43 PM\"></div><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c99d1c68-20dc-4efd-8116-34b9408b4192.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c99d1c68-20dc-4efd-8116-34b9408b4192.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><p>Player options now allow for:</p><ul><li>Disabling interaction with NPCs which will also hide the outline & icon</li></ul><ul><li>Overwriting conditions, allowing you to perform a hard set on the values instead of only adding/subtracting</li></ul><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/727a6a77-611b-43f9-b461-d62659b61e59.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/727a6a77-611b-43f9-b461-d62659b61e59.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><h3 id=\"changelog-962024\">9/6/2024</h3><ul><li>Updated Editor Utility</li></ul><p>Now all the variables are visible for branches and player choices</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/4f259800-e715-4137-bb04-8962f9aa4784.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/4f259800-e715-4137-bb04-8962f9aa4784.gif\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:50px\"></div><ul><li>Added inputs for changing player choice selection</li></ul><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/2f683bcf-8596-4cde-88f2-2016ec7f9981.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/2f683bcf-8596-4cde-88f2-2016ec7f9981.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><h3 id=\"changelog-882024\">8/8/2024</h3><ul><li>Fixed montage bug where player montage would play on NPC</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-6252024\">6/25/2024</h3><ul><li>Added Dialogue Editor Utility widget</li><li>Updated camera & activator variables to soft actor references, now allowing you to save referenced actors</li><li>Updated dialogue system from maps to arrays</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-3202024\">3/20/2024</h3><ul><li>Fixed explanation level dialogue that had clashing name replacement</li><li>Fixed explanation level auto-complete example would generate text block if player spammed input</li><li>Began working on new example NPC blueprint using 2 new camera components</li><li>Fixed alt buttons were not showing (made separate alt button widget) due to choice buttons clashing</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-292024\">2/9/2024</h3><ul><li>Added actor outline which highlights actor to talk to, when in range</li><li>Added dynamic name replacement – system will auto-populate names for speakers and when names are detected in dialogues</li><li>Added option to switch focused sprites during dialogues – darkens whoever isn’t talking</li><li>Updated editor functions & added nameplate & sprite function</li><li>Fixed sprite not showing unless using nameplate</li><li>Added “DC Owner” variable to replace ‘Get Owner” node</li><li>Fixed setting mesh variable so that any mesh, not just skeletal meshes will be detected</li><li>Fixed color for sprite tints (variable existed in struct but was not plugged into anything)</li><li>Added icon background as a variable in Icon struct</li><li>Added logic so if no icon background is placed, it will be transparent and still show the icon</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-v-22\">V 2.2</h3><ul><li>Added Changelog to track updates</li><li>Organized functions, macros, and variables</li><li>Added NPC location which moves NPC characters to selected location during dialogue, and will change dialogue when location is reached</li><li>Added validation to blueprint library functions resolving errors when simulating</li><li>Removed Paragon & Trooper materials & textures to reduce file size</li><li>Consolidated icon fade animation to 1 forward/reverse</li><li>Added bool for Location / 2D dialogue audio</li></ul>"
  }
 ]
};
